0: An explanation of the input/output parameters follows:
0: T/V    : Wall time / encoded variant.
0: N      : The order of the coefficient matrix A.
0: NB     : The partitioning blocking factor.
0: P      : The number of process rows.
0: Q      : The number of process columns.
0: Time   : Time in seconds to solve the linear system.
0: Gflops : Rate of execution for solving the linear system.
0: 
0: The following parameter values will be used:
0: 
0: N      :    4000 
0: NB     :     128 
0: PMAP   : Row-major process mapping
0: P      :       2 
0: Q      :       2 
0: PFACT  :   Right 
0: NBMIN  :       4 
0: NDIV   :       2 
0: RFACT  :   Crout 
0: BCAST  :  1ringM 
0: DEPTH  :       0 
0: SWAP   : Mix (threshold = 64)
0: L1     : transposed form
0: U      : transposed form
0: EQUIL  : yes
0: ALIGN  : 8 double precision words
0: 
0: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0: 
0: - The matrix A is randomly generated for each test.
0: - The following scaled residual check will be computed:
0:       ||Ax-b||_oo / ( eps * ( || x ||_oo * || A ||_oo + || b ||_oo ) * N )
0: - The relative machine precision (eps) is taken to be               1.110223e-16
0: - Computational tests pass if scaled residuals are less than                16.0
